.SS man
.TP
\fBcommands\fR
hogar\-shell(1) as roff, generated from this table
.TP
\fBconfig\fR
hogar\-shell(5) as roff, generated from the config schema
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/hogar-shell/config.toml
Everything, hot\-reloaded on save. Written annotated on first run.
.TP
.I ~/.config/hogar-shell/tokens.toml
Design\-token overrides. Deliberately unstable \- the config's
.B [theme]
section is the supported surface.
.TP
.I ~/.config/hogar-shell/monitors/<output>/config.toml
Per\-monitor overrides, same shape as the global file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/hogar-shell/state.json
Runtime state the shell owns, such as the current wallpaper. Not settings.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/hogar-shell/<instance>.sock
The command socket, one per compositor instance.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where the config directory is looked for; falls back to
.IR $HOME/.config .
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Where the command socket is created.
.TP
.B HYPRLAND_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE
Names the socket, so two compositors on one login session get one socket each. Outside Hyprland the
name is still stable and the client still finds the shell.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Log filter; defaults to
.BR info .
.SH EXAMPLES
Start the shell from the compositor:
.PP
.EX
exec\-once = hogar-shell
.EE
.PP
Bind an action to a key:
.PP
.EX
bind = SUPER, SPACE, exec, hogar-shell launcher
bind = SUPER, N, exec, hogar-shell panel toggle notifications
bind = , XF86AudioRaiseVolume, exec, hogar-shell volume up
.EE
.PP
Write a config with every key in it, then edit it down:
.PP
.EX
hogar-shell config schema > ~/.config/hogar-shell/config.toml
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hogar-shell (5)
